is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: spine_router_0_1
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: FRR BGP neighbor configuration on spine_router_0_1.

Mechanism: In eBGP, each side must configure the neighbor’s remote-as to match the other side’s local AS. The leaf (leaf_router_0_1) opens with local AS 65201, but the spine is configured to expect AS 65999. The spine therefore rejects the leaf’s OPEN with a “bad peer AS” error, causing the session to cycle and never reach Established.

Localization: The failing peering is between spine_router_0_1 (172.16.0.10/31 on eth2) and leaf_router_0_1 (172.16.0.11/31 on eth1). Evidence:
- leaf_router_0_1: router bgp 65201; neighbor 172.16.0.10 remote-as 65101 (correct) and “show ip bgp summary” shows 172.16.0.10 in Idle.
- spine_router_0_1 running config: router bgp 65101; neighbor 172.16.0.11 remote-as 65999 (incorrect). “show ip bgp summary” shows neighbor 172.16.0.11 AS 65999 in Idle.
All other fabric sessions are Established and reachability between 10.0.0.2 and 10.0.1.2 is intact via the other spine.

Root cause: A misconfigured remote-as on spine_router_0_1 for neighbor 172.16.0.11 was set to 65999 instead of the leaf’s AS 65201 during the morning config push.

Corrective fix: On spine_router_0_1, update the BGP neighbor to the correct AS and reset the session:
- vtysh: conf t; router bgp 65101; no neighbor 172.16.0.11 remote-as 65999; neighbor 172.16.0.11 remote-as 65201; end
- clear ip bgp 172.16.0.11
The session should then Establish and converge normally. === END ===